 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n**Unexpected Argument Error in C Source Generation**\n\n**Description**\nHello, I've encountered an issue when trying to generate C source code using the `generate_c_source` command. It seems that the function call to `generate()` is not accepting the `generate_fuzzer` argument, which is causing the process to terminate unexpectedly.\n\n**Steps to Reproduce**\n1. Use the `generate_c_source` command with the `--generate-fuzzer` option enabled.\n2. Ensure that the input database file and output directory are correctly specified.\n3. Run the command and observe the error message indicating an unexpected keyword argument.\n\n**Expected Behavior**\nThe command should successfully generate the C source files, including any fuzzer-related files if the `--generate-fuzzer` option is specified.\n\n**Actual Behavior**\nThe command fails with an error message: `SystemExit: error: generate() got an unexpected keyword argument 'generate_fuzzer'`.\n\n**Environment**\n- OS: [Your OS]\n- Python version: [Your Python version]\n- Additional context: [Any other relevant information]\n\n**Additional Context**\nThis issue seems to be related to the handling of the `generate_fuzzer` argument in the `generate()` function. Any guidance on resolving this would be appreciated.\n</issue>\n",
